# ---------------------------------
#   ports/shelves — the closed list of shelves under ports/core
# ---------------------------------
#
#   <id> <description>
#
# One shelf per line: its id, whitespace, then one line saying what belongs on
# it. Every port lives at exactly ports/core/<id>/<name>/, and <id> must be
# listed here; a listed shelf holds at least one port. A line starting with '#'
# and a blank line are skipped.
#
# An id is lowercase letters, digits and '-'. It is never `libs`: a source-less
# port hashes <portdir>/../../libs, and a shelf by that name would put the
# whole shelf into those ports' recipe hashes. It is never `core`, and never
# the name of a port: a shelf named after a port cannot be told from a loose
# port, and `kpkg meta <name>` run inside ports/core takes the name as that
# directory. The pre-push hook and testing/preflight.sh both refuse a
# misplaced recipe, an unlisted shelf, a reserved or badly spelled id, and a
# shelf named after a port; only testing/preflight.sh refuses a listed shelf
# that holds no port.
#
# The order is the one the ports catalogue and a packages.txt's shelf sections
# follow. A packages.d/ phase reads its <shelf>.txt files in byte order,
# whatever the order here.

